FILED s473t3 (Opus triage of the 79 CATALOG-only blessed rows), on main
d9a2aac0.  PRE-EXISTING.  Probe: scratch/s473t3/probes/p19-qr-deref-write.pl.

KEYS BEHIND IT (baselines/fail-baseline.tsv, 2 keys covering 7 TAP rows;
`sweep-diff.pl` keys on file+description, #1041):
  qr.t 23 (the EMPTY-description key: TAP rows 11, 12, 14, 16, 18)
  qr.t 17 `object is blessed` (TAP rows 13 and 17 of the three that share
          that description; TAP row 6 of the same key is the SV-identity
          shape -- `docs/not-supported.md` "Scalar copy does not preserve
          reference/SV identity" -- so that key's cause is compound)

REPRODUCER (perl 5.40.3 vs ./runpcl):
    sub r { return qr/Good/ }
    my $c = r(); my $d = r(); my $d1 = $d;
    $$d = 'Bad';
    print "11 \$\$d  = [", ($$d  // "undef"), "]\n";
    print "12 \$\$d1 = [", ($$d1 // "undef"), "]\n";
    print "13 ref d = [", ref($d), "]\n";
    print "14 \"\$d\"  = [$d]\n";
    my $e = bless qr/Faux Pie/, 'Stew';
    $$e = 'Fake!';
    print "16 \$\$e  = [", ($$e // "undef"), "]\n";
    print "17 ref e = [", ref($e), "]\n";
    print "18 \"\$e\"  = [$e]\n";
  perl: 11 [Bad]  12 [Bad]  13 [Regexp] 14 [Regexp=SCALAR(0x...)]
        16 [Fake!] 17 [Stew] 18 [Stew=SCALAR(0x...)]
  PCL : 11 [undef] 12 [(?^:Good)] 13 []  14 [Bad]
        16 [undef] 17 []       18 [Fake!]

MECHANISM: PCL's `$$qr = V` assigns V into the box that HOLDS the qr, rather
than into the qr's referent, so the object is destroyed: `ref` goes from
`Regexp`/`Stew` to `''`, `$$d` reads undef, and `"$d"` becomes the raw value
instead of `Regexp=SCALAR(0x...)`.  A second copy taken before the write
(`$d1`) is left with the ORIGINAL pattern, where perl (sharing the referent)
sees the new value -- the two halves of the same identity gap.
Fix area: the scalar-deref lvalue path in `cl/pcl-runtime.lisp` for a
`p-regex-match` box.

RELATED, MEASURED IN THE SAME PROBE (not a row of this task): after
`bless $qr, 'Pie'`, `"$qr"` is `(?^:Good)` in perl and `Pie=(?^:Good)` in PCL
-- blessing a qr// must not change its stringification.  Catalog:
sweep-bug-catalog.md qr.t "Stringification of blessed qr// objects".

CATALOG NOTE THIS REPLACES: sweep-bug-catalog.md qr.t, "PVLV deref
`${qr//}` (tests 11, 12, 16, 24, 25, 27, 31, 32, 37) ... Complex.  Not
supported."  The row numbers are stale and the shape is a WRITE, not a deref.

FAMILY: `docs/not-supported.md` "Scalar copy does not preserve reference/SV
identity"; sibling #1488 (the ref-TYPE half).
